# Constants and Utilities Patterns

## Constants Organization

Group related constants in [src/utils/constants.js](mdc:src/utils/constants.js):

```javascript
// Feature-specific constants with clear naming
export const TIMER_CONSTANTS = {
  ONGOING_TAB: "ongoing",
  BREAK_TAB: "break",
  TASK_TIME: 25 * 60, // in seconds
  SHORT_BREAK_TIME: 5 * 60,
  LONG_BREAK_TIME: 15 * 60,
};

// Database table references
export const SUPABASE_TABLES = {
  TASKS: "tasks_master",
  JOURNALS: "journals_master",
};

// Application modes
export const EDIT = "edit";
export const CREATE = "create";

// Status constants
export const STATUS = {
  LOADING: "loading",
  FETCHED: "fetched",
};
```

## Task Categories

```javascript
// Use icon mappings for consistent UI
export const TASK_CATEGORY_ICONS = {
  work: "💼",
  play: "🎮",
  learn: "📚",
  others: "🗂️",
  read: "📖",
  fitness: "🏃‍♂️",
};

// Structured category data
export const TASK_CATEGORIES = [
  {
    value: "work",
    label: "Work",
    icon: TASK_CATEGORY_ICONS.work,
  },
  // ... more categories
];
```

## Utility Functions

- Keep utilities pure and focused on single responsibilities
- Use descriptive function names: `arraysEqual`, `deepCopy`, `handleResponse`
- Include proper error handling and validation
- Export individual functions rather than default exports

## Data Validation Patterns

```javascript
// Safe array/object checking
if (!tasks || !Array.isArray(tasks)) {
  return [];
}

// Fallback values for calculations
const maxRank =
  tasks.length > 0 ? Math.max(...tasks.map((task) => task.rank)) : 0;

// String validation with trimming
const title = !title || title.trim().length <= 0 ? DEFAULT_TITLE : title;
```

## Default Values

```javascript
// Use constants for default form values
const DEFAULT_FORM_VALUES = {
  title: "",
  description: "",
  totalSessions: MIN_SESSIONS,
  category: "others",
};

const DEFAULT_TITLE = "Untitled Task";
```

## Success/Error Handling

```javascript
// HTTP status code constants
export const SUCCESS_STATUS_CODES = [200, 201, 202, 204];

// Error message constants
export const EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED_ERROR = "email_not_confirmed";
```

